  "worked_solution": "The general solution to this equation is the sum of the complementary function and a particular solution.\n\nFirst, we find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(t),$ which is the solution to the simple harmonic motion equation ${y}^{\u2033}+{\\omega }^{2}y=0.$\nIt can be written in three different forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\omega t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\omega t$\n\nIn our case\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\omega =1.\n$$\n\nThus, we have:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+\u03d5)$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t$\n\nNext, we find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t).$ The particular solution is of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061t).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution into the differential equation and equating coefficients, we find that $\\alpha =-1$ and $\\beta =0.$ So, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t+\u03d5)-t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t+\u03d5)-t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\n- ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+B\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t-t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t$\n\nOnly I matches the forms above. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
